.TH RECONFORGE 1 "August 2026" "ReconForge v1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reconforge \- First-level reconnaissance and security-assessment engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reconforge
[\fITARGET\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B reconforge
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ReconForge is a first-level reconnaissance and security-assessment framework designed for authorized penetration testing, security assessments, and lab environments. It combines network discovery, DNS intelligence, service-aware enumeration, web technology detection, content discovery, vulnerability intelligence, correlation, and clean reporting into one guided workflow.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Running \fBreconforge\fR without arguments launches the interactive mode, prompting for Target (IP or URL), Recon Mode (STANDARD or LOW-IMPACT), and Content Discovery Profile (COMMON, EXTENDED, or DEEP).

.SH TARGET USAGE
.B reconforge <IP>
.br
.B reconforge -u http://<TARGET>:<PORT>
.br
.B reconforge -u https://<TARGET>:<PORT>
.br
.B reconforge --url https://example.com

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --mode standard
STANDARD reconnaissance mode. Performs full first-level discovery including all TCP ports, service detection, default scripts, and OS identification.
.TP
.B --mode low-impact
LOW-IMPACT reconnaissance mode. Reduces scan intensity, avoids aggressive secondary passes, and observes rate limiting.
.TP
.B --version
Displays the installed ReconForge version (v1.0.0).
.TP
.B -h, --help
Displays command-line help and usage information.

.SH OFFLINE ANALYSIS
.B reconforge import <dir>
.br
Imports a directory of scan outputs and stores them in a session.
.br
.B reconforge analyze <file>
.br
Analyzes a single scan output file and normalizes findings.

.SH SESSIONS AND REPORTS
.B reconforge sessions
.br
Lists stored scan sessions.
.br
.B reconforge show <session_id>
.br
Displays terminal summary for a specific session (use \fBcurrent\fR for the latest session).
.br
.B reconforge report <session_id> [--format terminal|json|html] [--output <file>]
.br
Generates a report for a session.
.br
.B reconforge waf <session_id>
.br
Displays WAF and CDN analysis for a session.

.SH TOOL AVAILABILITY
.B reconforge tools
.br
Checks the availability of registered tool adapters and external binaries on the system.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
reconforge
reconforge 10.10.10.25
reconforge 10.10.10.25 --mode low-impact
reconforge -u http://10.10.10.25:80
reconforge sessions
reconforge show current
reconforge report current --format html
reconforge waf current
reconforge tools
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error.

